.\"FILE    : pam.1"
.TH pam 1
.SH NAME
.B pam
- Dirac job control script
.SH SYNOPSIS
pam [-mw "mem"] [-nw "mem"] [-basdir "directory"] [-run "name"]
[-wrkdir "directory"] [-clean] [-keepwrk]
[-copy "file1 file2 ..."] [-get "file1 file2"] [-incmo] [-outcmo] [-infck] [-outfck]
[-mpi "n"] [-mpiarg "string"] [-machinefile "file"]
[-nice] [-notify] [-user "user"] [-dirac "cmd"] [-debug] [-help]
mol[.mol] menu[.inp]

.SH DESCRIPTION
.B pam
is the job control script to Dirac. It copies files to scratch work area directory,
starts
.B
DIRAC,
and moves files back, etc.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP 5
.B -mw "mem"
Set working memory (in megawords) for master. The size of the working memory
can also be specified through the environment variable
.B DIRWRK.
If this is not set, the default memory size specified in
.B configure
is used.
.TP 5
.B -basdir "directory"
Prepend directory to directory search list for finding basis sets.
May be repeated.
.TP 5
.B -run "name"
File suffix for output file. The default is ".out".
.TP 5
.B -wrkdir "directory"
Set directory for scratch work area. Default scratch directory is defined when configuring
.B Dirac.
.TP 5
.B -clean
Delete directory with scratch work area before starting job.
.TP 5
.B -keepwrk
Keep directory with scratch work area when job is finished
(default is to delete it unless Dirac exits abnormally).
.TP 5
.B -copy file
Copy file 'file' to work area
If
.B
-copy
is specified more than once, all files specified will be copied.
.TP 5
.B -get file
Get file 'file' from work area.
.B
-get
is incremental, just as
.B
-copy
.TP 5
.B -incmo
Copy file 'DFCOEF' (DHF molecular orbital coefficients) to work area. This is an alias for
.B -copy DFCOEF
.TP 5
.B -outcmo
Get file 'DFCOEF' (DHF molecular orbital coefficients) from work area. This is an alias for
.B -get DFCOEF
.TP 5
.B -infck
Copy file 'DFFCK2' to work area, for restart on 2-electron Fock matrix. This is an alias for
.B -copy DFFCK2
.TP 5
.B -outfck
Get file 'DFFCK2' from work area. This is an alias for
.B -get DFFCK2
.TP 5
.B -mpi "n"
Execute parallel version of
.B Dirac
with n nodes using MPI (default is sequential run, i.e. n = 1)
.TP 5
.B -mpiarg "string"
Any other arguments to be MPI in parallel runs.
.TP 5
.B -machinefile "file"
Specify file with list of machines to be used in MPI parallel runs.
.TP 5
.B -nw "mem"
Set working memory (in megawords) for slave nodes in parallel runs.
The size of the working memory
can also be specified through the environment variable
.B DIRNOD.
If neither
.B -nw
nor
.B DIRNOD
are set, then the memory size from
.B -mw
or
.B DIRWRK
is used. If none of these are set, the default memory size is used.
.TP 5
.B -nice
Execute the job with 'nice' or 'npri' (on SGI).
.TP 5
.B -notify
Send user a mail upon completion of the job.
.TP 5
.B -user "user"
Send the above e-mail to "user".
.TP 5
.B -dirac "cmd"
Use alternate 
.B Dirac executable
"cmd" instead of the default 
.B dirac.x.
.TP 5
.B -debug
Run 
.B DIRAC
in debugger
.TP 5
.B -help
This page.
.TP 5
.B mol[.mol]
The molecule file (must be given).
.TP 5
.B menu[.inp]
The Dirac menu (job) file (must be given).
Refer to the manual on
.B http://dirac.chem.sdu.dk
for a description of the files.
.PP
.SH FILES
pam
.SH BUGS
The path to the correct "mpirun" command is not automatically configured, you may have to edit pam to correct for this.
